October 10, 2026 (merge of weimingtom/MMP v0.2.1):
-Rebased the modernisation onto upstream v0.2.1 (IK angle limits, type 2
 rigid bodies, D3D->OpenGL conversion fixes, VMD writer, more VMD
 sections, glm_helper + test)
-Fixed buffer over-reads in the v0.2.1 SJIS/UTF-8 conversion (which also
 aborted on ASCII-only names) and in the VMD writer
-Animation/physics now step by wall-clock time (1/60 s) instead of once
 per rendered frame
-Dropped the OpenGL 3.0 #version 130 shader rewrite (used tmpnam); OpenGL
 3.2 core is required
-Implemented PMX rotation/translation inheritance (付与): leg D bones
 (足D/ひざD/足首D), 腰キャンセル, 肩C and eyes now follow their source bones
-Bone local transforms are rebuilt from the animation every frame, so IK
 links without keyframes (腕W/ひじW etc.) no longer accumulate twist
 (arms looked thin)
-libmmp.h no longer includes the viewer-only glfw_func_callbacks.h

October 10, 2026:
-Ported from GLFW 2 to GLFW 3 (GLFW 2 is no longer shipped by distributions)
-Updated for current GLM (0.9.9 / 1.x): radians everywhere, identity
 default constructors, GLM_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL
-Shaders now target OpenGL 3.3 core (#version 330, texture() instead of
 texture2D()) so they compile on Mesa; dropped ARB uniform entry points
-Fixed buffer over-reads in VMD/PMX text decoding, texture index -1 crash,
 shared toon texture off-by-one, missing-texture crash
-Case-insensitive texture lookup for models made on Windows
-Resizable window, aspect ratio follows the framebuffer
-Build system: pkg-config for dependencies, headers installed under
 include/libmmp, generated autotools files removed (run ./autogen.sh)
-Added Debian packaging
-Bone matrices are passed through a texture buffer instead of a
 uniform array limited to 254 bones (models with more bones showed
 spikes and garbage polygons, e.g. around skirts)
-PMX vertex indices of size 1/2 are now read as unsigned; models with
 more than 32767 vertices crashed in vertex morphs (segfault)
-Guard keyframe interpolation against duplicate keys

January 12, 2014:
-removed model data file from git repo history
-Updated README with info on libglm,libglew,
-Fixed bug that caused SDL2/SDL2_mixer to be required even with enable-sound turned off (or SDL2/SDL2_mixer unavailable)

January 11, 2014: ver 0.1 release
